# Rebuildable output only (repo-standards.md: never commit build output).
/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# The ENG7 persistent result cache (FS3): regenerable, non-authoritative derived data that lives in a
# `.cache/` sub-folder of any workbook — deleting it never changes a value (VAL2). It is written
# whenever an evaluating command runs (including tests over the committed conformance fixtures), so it
# is never tracked; a workbook's `.cache/` is always rebuilt on demand.
**/.cache/

# The python venv used to AUTHOR the ingest fixtures is disposable — the generated fixtures
# (charlie-ingest/tests/fixtures/*.{ods,xlsx}) ARE committed, so the Rust tests need no
# python/odfpy/openpyxl.
charlie-ingest/.fixture-venv/
**/__pycache__/
